  wonders: "First met here: mortise marks, a saying, “Chalk is cheaper than oak”, load-beetles, the listening mallet and load-bells."
  met: "Met here for the first time: BoneWAP."
  palette: "Its palette is the land tree, earned a layer at a time: violet and magenta: three lands branching from one trunk."
  berries: "A boneberry in this chapter tastes of rib tips."
  harmonies: "The joiners carried the bushes over the pass. The crack's note and the frame's note keep one law. The frame's note reaches the well. A boneberry promises nothing, and feeds you. A boonberry pie is never smaller. The egg rides against her ribs."
